Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 4.3  Red knot \[LongDash] monthly population centroid restricted to \
the Americas flyway. Compare this coherent loop with the broken global \
centroid (the ",
 StyleBox["knotGlobal",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " contrast above), which would sit uselessly in the mid-Atlantic, ~4,670 \
km/month from this track. ",
 StyleBox["A caveat in the other direction:",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " presence weighting blunts but does not erase effort bias. The Americas \
winter centroid here sits around Panama/northern Colombia rather than at the \
iconic ",
 StyleBox["rufa",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " wintering grounds in Tierra del Fuego (~54\[Degree]S): the densely-birded \
USA and Caribbean still outweigh the sparsely-observed Patagonian coast, and \
the centroid blends several wintering areas. The shape of the journey is \
right; the precise southern extreme is pulled north."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"c2dde831-1b26-4724-be08-c5974c212082"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
4.1  Is the seasonal loop real, or just where the birders are?\
\>", "Subsection",
 FontFamily->"Roboto Condensed",
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.153, 0.51, 0.64],ExpressionUUID->"f26e67b1-430c-4958-9222-0d120bd4fd82"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A fair challenge to everything so far: perhaps these loops are not \
migration at all, but the seasonal pattern of where ",
 StyleBox["observers",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " happen to be. We can test that head-on. Take each species' occurrences, ",
 StyleBox["shuffle the month labels",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " \[LongDash] every record keeps its location but is reassigned a random \
month \[LongDash] and recompute the centroid loop. Repeat 500 times. If the \
apparent migration were a sampling artifact, the shuffled loops would swing \
as widely as the real one; if it is real, the true loop's north\[Dash]south \
span will sit far beyond anything the shuffles produce."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"c859c3df-ec07-4503-b98f-c8211e1620c9"],

